The attached image (Figure 4) demonstrates the active transport and uptake of Nano-11 nanoparticles by antigen-presenting cells (APCs) in draining lymph nodes. Flow cytometry plots and a line graph (A, B) show that Nano-11-containing myeloid cells peak in number at Day 2 post-injection, gradually decreasing by Day 7. Bar charts (C, D) further reveal that migratory dendritic cells (MigDCs) account for the highest percentage of Nano-11-positive cells and exhibit the highest mean fluorescence intensity per cell, indicating their efficient uptake of Nano-11. This active targeting of MigDCs by Nano-11 is crucial for its role as an effective vaccine adjuvant.